Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Program: workstream 09's capacity instructions
 (capacity-preview) [skip ci]

frontier_abi::capacity (feature capacity-preview): the fourteen
instructions on workstream 4's provisional band 0xF0-0xFD, their exact
encodings, their account lists, the with-seed addresses of the pool
(`cp`) and job (`cj`) accounts off the Season, the program errors
109 + code (110-139), and the proposed 0x2000 program-version bit.

permutation-frontier (feature capacity-preview): proc::capacity, routed
before the v2 tags as the wide preview is, so a default build refuses
the bytes as before. Every check is the rules' (frontier::capacity);
the handlers read the facility from its Holding (generation, owner, the
capture's previous generation and bell), change the Holding's own
production on LendCapacity and ReclaimCapacity (core patch 0001), take
DepositToJob's goods from the user's vault in the facility's province
and put ClaimJob's back there (refused whole past CAP - CUSTODY_QUOTA),
credit a captor's share into the Holding's stores on
RecordFacilityLoss, create and close the pool and job accounts (rent
back to its payer). A Season of another build is refused. No PS2 record
(workstream 09's record kinds are not allocated); a released generation
or one that moved twice before the loss was recorded cannot be dated
from the Holding, so RecordFacilityLoss refuses it (NotImplemented).

Host tests through the real dispatch (map_growth_runtime_tests'
world, no key generated, derived or signed; is_signer set by the
test): the whole path from A's first home (PlaceHome) to B's claimed
arms and the retired job, refusals that change nothing, resends, a
capture where the captor takes what is at the facility, and a Season of
another build. Two shared guards name the preview explicitly:
ix.rs's list of vault-stock writers gains the capacity writer (it
clamps to CAP - CUSTODY_QUOTA), and the rules' ruleset-binding test
names the capacity module as an unbound preview (its version is
workstream 4's to give). The previous commit left that rules test
failing; this one fixes it.

Tests: permutation-rules 513 (515 with the feature), frontier-abi 146
(151), permutation-frontier 107 default, 111 capacity-preview, 108
custody-preview, 112 both; clippy -D warnings and fmt on the changed
files. SBF, LiteSVM and the verifier's tests are not run.

